-- title:
--   Corner ring ≅ local Hecke algebra at auxiliary level Mr
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a complete discrete valuation ring which is a domain of characteristic zero with finite residue field, $p \neq 2$ a prime lying in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal O$, and $\bar\rho$ a two-dimensional representation of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ over the residue field, factoring through a finite extension and absolutely irreducible (irreducible after base change to an algebraic closure). Let $S$ be a finite set of primes containing $p$, and $M$ a nonzero level all of whose prime divisors lie in $S$, with $p^2 \nmid M$; let $S_{\min} \subseteq S$ contain $p$ and consist, away from $p$, exactly of the primes where $\bar\rho$ is ramified, each such prime dividing $M$, primes $q \neq p$ dividing $M$ but outside $S_{\min}$ dividing it exactly to the second power, no $q^3$ with $q \neq p$ dividing $M$, $\bar\rho$ unipotent on inertia at each $q \in S_{\min}$, $q \neq p$ (characteristic polynomial $(X-1)^2$ there), and $\bar\rho$ ordinary at $p$ whenever $p \mid M$. Let $r$ be a prime outside $S$ not dividing $M$ with $p \nmid r-1$ such that for every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $r$ a nonunit and every Frobenius element $\sigma$ at $r$ for $P$ one has $\operatorname{tr}\bar\rho(\sigma)^2 \neq (r+1)^2$. Assume weight-two cusp forms of level $\Gamma_0(M)$ are spanned over $\mathbb C$ by those with integral $q$-expansion coefficients, and let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from the Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra M 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) (the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra generated by the $T_\ell$, $\ell \nmid M$, $\ell \notin S$, and the $U_q$, $q \mid M$, $q \notin S$) to the residue field with $\operatorname{charpoly}\bar\rho(\sigma) = X^2 - \theta(T_\ell)X + \ell$ for all primes $\ell \nmid M$, $\ell \notin S$ and all Frobenius elements $\sigma$ at $\ell$. Put $L = Mr$ and let $H \le (\mathbb Z/L)^\times$ be the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb Z/r)$, so that $H^1 =$ `H1 L H 𝒪` is the group of additive maps from $\Gamma_H(L)$ to $\mathcal O$. Let $\mathbb T$ be a commutative $\mathcal O$-algebra, module-finite over $\mathcal O$, acting $\mathcal O$-compatibly on $H^1$, let $\mathrm{Sp}$ be an idempotent splitting of $\mathbb T$ (complete orthogonal idempotents $e_j$ together with maximal ideals $\mathfrak m_j$ exhausting the maximal ideals, with $e_j \in \mathfrak m_k$ iff $j \neq k$) and $i$ an index such that the corner submodule $e_i H^1$ is finite and free over $\mathcal O$. Let $t$ and $c$ assign to each Hecke generator of level $L$ outside $S$ an element of $\mathbb T$ and of $\mathcal O$ respectively, subject to: every element of $\mathbb T$ acts on $H^1$ through the $\mathcal O$-subalgebra generated by the operators `opFamily` attached to the guarded generators (those $g$ for which $g = U_q$ forces $q \mid M$); for guarded $g$, $t(g)$ acts as `opFamily` at $g$ and $t(g) - c(g) \in \mathfrak m_i$; any $v \in H^1$ such that for every guarded $g$ and every $k$ some power $(t(g)-c(g))^n v$ lies in $\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}^k H^1$ already lies in $e_i H^1$; the residue of $c(T_\ell)$ equals $\theta(T_\ell)$ for primes $\ell$ dividing neither $M$ nor $L$ and outside $S$; $c(U_q)$ lies in the maximal ideal for $q \mid L$ with $q \mid M$, $q \neq p$, $q^2 \mid M$; $c(U_p)$ is a unit when $p \mid L$ and $p \mid M$; and $c(\langle d \rangle) \equiv 1$ modulo the maximal ideal for all $d$. Assume finally $e_i H^1 \neq 0$ and that the corner ring $e_i \mathbb T e_i$ acts faithfully on $e_i H^1$. Then there is an isomorphism $e$ of $\mathcal O$-algebras from the corner ring onto the localised Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeLocal M S 𝒪 θ`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131) such that for every prime $\ell$ dividing neither $M$ nor $L$ and outside $S$, and every $m \in e_i H^1$, the element $e^{-1}(\pi(T_\ell)) \cdot m$ coincides, as an element of $H^1$, with `heckeT L H ℓ` applied to $m$.
--
--   This is a multiplicity-one statement of Taylor–Wiles type at an auxiliary level $L = Mr$: the corner of the abstract Hecke-type algebra $\mathbb T$ cut out by an idempotent of the splitting is identified, compatibly with the anaemic Hecke operators $T_\ell$ acting on the cohomology carrier, with the local Hecke algebra attached to the mod-$p$ eigensystem $\theta$ of $\bar\rho$ at level $M$. It is used by the level-raising packages at $p$ that build corner data and pairings at levels $Nr$ and $Nrp$.
